If a file is ambiguous, the following rule applies:
  - .md, .txt, .rst                      -> CC BY-NC 4.0 (this license)
  - .py, .go, .sh, .ps1                  -> MIT
  - .yml (GitHub Actions workflows)      -> MIT

Note: the rule above is file-type based. Markdown documentation inside
tools/ (e.g. tools/python/README.md, tools/python/Session_Report.md) is
CC BY-NC 4.0 like all other .md files in this repository, even though the
source code in the same directories is MIT. tools/LICENSE contains the
MIT text that applies to source code under tools/.

